# Dev-stack secrets for the whisper-wazuh connector.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) in THIS directory — docker compose reads `.env` from the
# compose file's directory, not the repo root:
#
#     cp dev/wazuh-single-node/.env.example dev/wazuh-single-node/.env
#     # then edit .env and set your key
#
# The Whisper API key is injected into the manager container's environment
# (docker-compose.yml `WHISPER_API_KEY=${WHISPER_API_KEY:-}`), which the custom-whisper
# connector reads first (env → /var/ossec/etc/whisper.key → argv). Because compose
# re-injects it on every `up`, it survives `make dev-reset` — unlike the in-container
# key file. Leave it blank to fall back to the key file.

WHISPER_API_KEY=